\paragraph{Held-out validation.}
\label{sec:scs-validation}
On the FewRel validation split (16 relation types fully disjoint from the 64 training-pool types), pairwise SCS--confusion Spearman correlation remains positive and significant ($\rho = 0.470$, $p < 10^{-7}$, $n = 120$ pairs), stronger than the training pool ($\rho = 0.158$), ruling out training-set contamination as the driver of the observed relationship.

