\paragraph{Held-out validation.}
\label{sec:scs-validation}
From the 80-type confusion matrix, we extract the $\binom{16}{2} = 120$ pairs among the 16 validation-origin types (fully disjoint from the 64 training-pool types). The SCS--confusion Spearman correlation remains positive and significant ($\rho = 0.216$, $p = 0.018$), nearly identical to the full 80-type pool ($\rho = 0.218$, $p < 10^{-34}$, $n = 3{,}160$ pairs), ruling out training-set contamination as the driver of the observed relationship.
